WEBVTT

00:00:08.857 --> 00:00:12.937
Hud saw something in you
that you don't even see in yourself.

00:00:14.697 --> 00:00:16.657
Are you ready to go find it?

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:18.977
Yes, sir.

00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:29.577
All right, all right. Bring it back.

00:00:29.617 --> 00:00:31.937
(McQUEEN PANTING)

00:00:32.657 --> 00:00:35.777
Lesson one: You're old. Accept it.

00:00:35.977 --> 00:00:38.257
-I told him that.
-He's probably losing his hearing.

00:00:38.297 --> 00:00:39.897
(SHOUTING)
He said you're old and losing--

00:00:39.977 --> 00:00:41.057
I heard him.

00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:43.377
You'll never be as fast as Storm,

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.217
but you can be smarter than him.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:47.737
Okay, what do I do?

00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:50.177
They said you were
in a demolition derby.

00:00:50.337 --> 00:00:51.897
Yeah, it was terrible and I almost--

00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:54.497
Are you sure?
Because there's not a scratch on you.

00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:00.497
Funny what a racer can do
when he's not over-thinking things.

00:01:02.697 --> 00:01:04.817
SHANNON: Shannon Spokes
here at Florida International,

00:01:04.857 --> 00:01:06.057
where Jackson Storm...

00:01:06.257 --> 00:01:09.337
clocked 214 miles per hour today.

00:01:14.257 --> 00:01:17.337
SMOKEY: You want to beat Storm,
you need someone to stand in for him.

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:19.017
Like a sparring partner.

00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:23.017
I'm not so sure. Not a racer.
(CHUCKLES) Just a trainer!

00:01:23.177 --> 00:01:24.097
Go ahead and gun it.

00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:27.497
(ENGINE REVVING)

00:01:29.057 --> 00:01:30.577
-Oh, yeah!
-(SMOKEY CHUCKLES)

00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:33.097
With no muffler
you even sound like Storm.

00:01:33.897 --> 00:01:36.017
Oh, you're going down, McQueen!

00:01:36.177 --> 00:01:38.337
Get that arthritis-riddled keister
onto the track

00:01:38.537 --> 00:01:41.377
so I can put you into...
the old folks' home against your will!

00:01:43.017 --> 00:01:43.897
How was that?

00:01:44.697 --> 00:01:46.257
-That'll work.
-Worked for me.

00:01:46.457 --> 00:01:47.937
-I'm good.
-Yep. That'll do.

00:01:48.097 --> 00:01:48.777
Did you hear what she said?

00:01:49.617 --> 00:01:52.217
SMOKEY: You didn't show up
in Florida for qualifying

00:01:52.297 --> 00:01:54.097
so you'll be starting last.

00:01:54.737 --> 00:01:56.497
I'll give you three laps to catch her.

00:01:56.737 --> 00:01:59.297
Go through the entire field in three laps?

00:01:59.857 --> 00:02:01.057
You want to beat Storm or not?

00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:04.737
-Yes! Of course I do.
-Well, then, go!

00:02:05.177 --> 00:02:06.337
(CRUZ SQUEALS)

00:02:06.377 --> 00:02:07.537
Come on, kid.

00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.457
All right. Looks like
we got some work to do.

00:02:22.097 --> 00:02:25.457
Look alive. The reflexes
are the first thing to go.

00:02:25.697 --> 00:02:27.537
(EXCLAIMING)

00:02:28.177 --> 00:02:30.057
-Ah!
-(MOOING)

00:02:31.497 --> 00:02:32.737
McQUEEN: Why are we in a field?

00:02:33.337 --> 00:02:35.257
Sneak through that window!

00:02:35.337 --> 00:02:36.977
-What does that mean?
-I don't know.

00:02:37.137 --> 00:02:37.817
-Go!
-(HONKS)

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:40.497
(BOTH SCREAM)

00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:44.417
McQUEEN: Whoa!

00:02:47.297 --> 00:02:49.577
CRUZ: Not cool, man. Not cool!

00:02:53.977 --> 00:02:55.097
Let's run it back.

00:02:57.537 --> 00:02:59.457
Do you even want to be out here?

00:03:02.297 --> 00:03:03.897
Only two days left, kid.

00:03:03.937 --> 00:03:05.937
-You got to work harder.
-(GRUNTING)

00:03:09.697 --> 00:03:10.977
Wait, wait, who was that?

00:03:11.137 --> 00:03:12.377
I put McQueen in there.

00:03:12.457 --> 00:03:13.937
Give you some real competition.

00:03:15.377 --> 00:03:16.777
(BOTH LAUGH)

00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:19.937
SMOKEY: Hud was a master
of letting the other cars

00:03:20.097 --> 00:03:21.257
do the work for him.

00:03:21.297 --> 00:03:22.377
RIVER: He used to say

00:03:22.457 --> 00:03:24.057
cling to 'em like you was
two June bugs...

00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:25.457
on a summer night.

00:03:25.617 --> 00:03:26.897
-He stole that from me.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:03:27.377 --> 00:03:29.817
Drafting? I've never had to do that.

00:03:29.857 --> 00:03:32.457
Yeah, that's when you were fast.

00:03:32.497 --> 00:03:33.897
Now you're slow.

00:03:33.977 --> 00:03:35.697
-RIVER: And old.
-And rickety.

00:03:35.777 --> 00:03:37.657
-And dilapidated.
-Okay! Okay, I get it.

00:03:37.697 --> 00:03:39.977
The new you has to
look for opportunities...

00:03:40.017 --> 00:03:41.817
you never knew were there.

00:03:43.617 --> 00:03:44.777
(MOOING)

00:03:44.817 --> 00:03:46.977
-Sneak through the window!
-(BOTH EXCLAIM)

00:03:48.697 --> 00:03:49.977
Sneak through the window.

00:03:50.057 --> 00:03:51.097
What?

00:03:51.137 --> 00:03:53.417
When a window opens, take it!

00:03:54.817 --> 00:03:55.817
(McQUEEN WHOOPS)

00:03:58.657 --> 00:03:59.657
Whoa!

00:04:02.817 --> 00:04:03.577
Yes.

00:04:04.617 --> 00:04:07.257
-Whoa! I made it!
-All right!

00:04:07.497 --> 00:04:08.497
(BOTH EXCLAIM)

00:04:08.817 --> 00:04:10.177
Let's go! Let's move!

00:04:11.457 --> 00:04:12.457
-(GUIDO GRUNTING)
-SMOKEY: Reflexes!

00:04:14.337 --> 00:04:16.017
All right, Guido, turn up the heat.

00:04:16.217 --> 00:04:17.177
GUIDO: Okay.

00:04:17.897 --> 00:04:19.217
Whoa! Whoa!

00:04:20.297 --> 00:04:21.297
(GASPS)

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.617
All right, look who finally showed up.

00:04:29.857 --> 00:04:31.937
SMOKEY: This is where
we cut our racing teeth.

00:04:32.177 --> 00:04:33.577
In the woods?

00:04:33.737 --> 00:04:37.497
Let's just say the moon
was always shining on us.

00:04:37.537 --> 00:04:38.537
Huh?

00:04:38.617 --> 00:04:41.417
If the moon didn't shine,
we didn't have to--

00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:42.537
Oh, never mind.

00:04:42.577 --> 00:04:44.377
JUNIOR MOON:
We ran moonshine, dummy!

00:04:44.457 --> 00:04:45.497
Oh!

00:04:45.857 --> 00:04:48.897
By the way, no lights. Instinct only.

00:04:49.697 --> 00:04:50.697
(ALL WHOOPING)

00:04:51.377 --> 00:04:52.057
CRUZ: Yeah!

00:04:54.297 --> 00:04:55.417
(CRUZ EXCLAIMING)

00:04:56.377 --> 00:04:57.537
RIVER: Yeah!

00:04:59.737 --> 00:05:00.777
(GASPING)

00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:03.057
Oh!

00:05:04.977 --> 00:05:06.017
(GRUNTS)

00:05:08.137 --> 00:05:09.177
Whoa!

00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:10.897
(CHUCKLES) Yeah!

00:05:11.417 --> 00:05:12.417
(WHOOPING)

00:05:16.577 --> 00:05:17.697
Whoo-hoo!

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:22.337
(CRUZ WHOOPS AND LAUGHS)

00:05:24.337 --> 00:05:24.977
McQUEEN: All right!

00:05:33.457 --> 00:05:34.577
(McQUEEN WHOOPING)

00:05:37.417 --> 00:05:38.537
McQueen's still not here?

00:05:38.577 --> 00:05:40.257
Didn't he pull this
when he was a rookie?

00:05:40.417 --> 00:05:42.297
At least that's what
my grandfather told me.

00:05:42.817 --> 00:05:44.937
SMOKEY: All right, we got
time for one last race.

00:05:45.937 --> 00:05:48.617
Hurry this along, boss,
we got to get you to Florida.

00:05:48.777 --> 00:05:49.897
Go!

00:05:54.137 --> 00:05:57.777
Maybe it's best that he doesn't show up,
after how last season ended.

00:06:02.137 --> 00:06:03.377
Let me put it this way.

00:06:03.537 --> 00:06:06.657
I'm not losing any sleep
wondering where Lightning McQueen is.

00:06:12.137 --> 00:06:13.457
Come on, boy. Come on!

00:06:21.497 --> 00:06:23.297
SMOKEY: All right, McQueen.
There you go, boy!

00:06:23.457 --> 00:06:24.897
There you go.

